%
%  Ex_FormationFlying_SSO_FEEP
%
%  Delta-V budget for a two-satellite formation in a sun-synchronous orbit
%  (SSO) over 5 years, with FEEP (field emission electric propulsion)
%  thrusters. FEEP can only fire continuously at low thrust, so there are no
%  impulsive burns anywhere in this script: every manoeuvre is a finite burn,
%  throttled with the thruster DutyCycle and held for a whole control cycle.
%
%  FORMATION REQUIREMENT (RTN frame centred on Sat1, Sat2 relative to Sat1)
%     Along-track (T) separation :  50 ... 1000 km
%     Normal (N) separation      :  200 km (amplitude, see below)
%
%  The normal separation is created with a RAAN (LTAN) offset between the two
%  planes, NOT with an inclination difference. Both satellites have the same
%  a, e, i, so their J2 nodal precession is identical (both are sun-
%  synchronous) and the offset is passively stable. A constant 200 km N offset
%  is not possible in orbit, so "200 km normal" is taken as the amplitude of
%  the N component, which swings +/-200 km over each orbit:
%        A_N = a * sqrt( di^2 + (sin(i) * dRAAN)^2 )  =  NAmp
%
%  ASSUMPTIONS (all editable below)
%     560 km circular SSO, LTAN 10:30, start 01 Jan 2027, 5 years (1826 days)
%     2 identical 400 kg satellites (395 kg dry + 5 kg propellant), Cd 2.2;
%     Sat2 has 10 % more drag area (2.2 vs 2.0 m^2) to exercise the
%     differential-drag control
%     FEEP: 4 mN per thruster (a cluster of four 1 mN heads), Isp 3000 s, one
%     prograde and two out-of-plane (+N / -N) thrusters per satellite, power
%     never limits thrust
%     Gravity 8x8, Sun + Moon, SRP, NRLMSISE-00 drag with the Schatten
%     nominal solar-cycle prediction
%     The satellites start in their formation slots (launcher / acquisition
%     manoeuvres are not in the budget)
%
%  CONTROL (one cycle = 15 orbits, about 1.000 day)
%     1. Altitude : each satellite tracks a target mean SMA with a PI law on
%                   continuous prograde thrust (drag make-up; the integral
%                   term learns the drag acceleration).
%     2. Along-track : when T leaves [TLow, THigh] a drift back towards the
%                   centre is commanded, then stopped at TCenter. Drift rate
%                   is measured from T, and the SMA offset needed to get the
%                   commanded rate is split between the satellites (the
%                   thrusters are prograde only, so the one that has to be
%                   higher is raised).
%     3. Inclination : HoldSSO = 1: each satellite holds the mean inclination
%                   that gives exactly the sun-synchronous nodal rate. When the
%                   error exceeds iDead, both do an out-of-plane campaign with
%                   sign(cos(u)) thrust (flipped at the polar points).
%                   HoldSSO = 0: no absolute control; Sat2 only follows the
%                   inclination of Sat1 (campaigns when it differs by more
%                   than iDeadRel), so the two planes keep precessing together.
%                   In both cases the RAAN offset is trimmed with a small
%                   differential inclination if the N amplitude has drifted.
%     The controller uses Brouwer-Lyddane mean elements referred to the
%     true-of-date equator, averaged over the 15 orbits of the cycle.
%
%  DELTA-V ACCOUNTING
%     Integrated from thrust/mass for every burn, separately for the
%     tangential (altitude + along-track) and normal (inclination) thrusters,
%     and cross-checked against the rocket equation from the propellant used
%     (dvRkt1/2 must equal dvT + dvN of the same satellite).
%
%  OUTPUT (GMAT output folder)
%     FormationSSO_FEEP_Daily.txt     one row per control cycle
%     FormationSSO_FEEP_Summary.txt   delta-V budget and compliance summary
%        dvT1/dvN1/dvT2/dvN2 : tangential / normal delta-V of Sat1 / Sat2, m/s
%        dvTot               : total for the formation, m/s
%        TMin/TMax           : along-track separation extremes, km
%        ANMin/ANMax         : normal-separation amplitude extremes, km
%        nOutT/nOutN         : cycles outside 50..1000 km / 180..220 km
%        epMax               : largest epoch difference between the satellites, s
%
%  REFERENCE RESULTS below are from the earlier 600 km, 51 kg, 1 mN case and are
%  being re-run for the current 560 km, 400 kg, 4 mN parameters.
%  (GMAT R2026a, 5 years, delta-V in m/s)
%                              Sat1 tang  Sat1 norm  Sat2 tang  Sat2 norm  Formation
%   HoldSSO = 0 (default: the orbit plane is allowed to drift)
%     Schatten nominal              2.5        0.0        2.7        4.5        9.7
%     +2 sigma, late cycle          6.1        0.0        6.8        3.4       16.3
%   HoldSSO = 1 (sun-synchronous inclination and LTAN held)
%     Schatten nominal              2.5       31.5        2.7       29.7       66.5
%     +2 sigma, late cycle          6.2       31.4        6.8       29.6       74.0
%   tang = altitude + along-track, norm = inclination / node control.
%   Along-track stays within 289..531 km (limit 50..1000 km) and the N amplitude
%   within 198..206 km in all four cases. 4..18 g of propellant per satellite.
%   With HoldSSO = 0 the inclination falls from 97.81 to 97.62 deg (Sun and Moon)
%   and the LTAN drifts from 10:30 to about 09:10 over the 5 years; with
%   HoldSSO = 1 it stays within 1.3 min. Without any control the same pair drifts
%   out of the corridor in about a year.
%
%  Run time is about 30 min for 5 years in GmatConsole (about 1 s per day).
%  Plots and a budget table from the output files: plot_formation_results.py
%  (same folder), e.g.  python plot_formation_results.py <GMAT output folder>
%  Set ControlOn = 0 for the uncontrolled (free-drift) reference case.
%

%----------------------------------------
%---------- Spacecraft
%----------------------------------------

% Both satellites are defined by mean (Brouwer-Lyddane) elements in the Earth
% true-of-date frame. The orbit and formation geometry are set at the start of
% the mission sequence from the design parameters.
Create Spacecraft Sat1;
Sat1.DateFormat       = UTCGregorian;
Sat1.Epoch            = '01 Jan 2027 00:00:00.000';
Sat1.CoordinateSystem = EarthTOD;
Sat1.DisplayStateType = BrouwerMeanShort;
Sat1.BrouwerShortSMA  = 6938.137;
Sat1.BrouwerShortECC  = 0.0012;
Sat1.BrouwerShortINC  = 97.7876;
Sat1.BrouwerShortRAAN = 258.7256;
Sat1.BrouwerShortAOP  = 90;
Sat1.BrouwerShortMA   = 0;
Sat1.DryMass          = 395;
Sat1.Cd               = 2.2;
Sat1.Cr               = 1.3;
Sat1.DragArea         = 2.0;
Sat1.SRPArea          = 2.0;
Sat1.Tanks            = {Tank1};
Sat1.Thrusters        = {FeepT1, FeepNp1, FeepNm1};
Sat1.PowerSystem      = FeepPower;

Create Spacecraft Sat2;
Sat2.DateFormat       = UTCGregorian;
Sat2.Epoch            = '01 Jan 2027 00:00:00.000';
Sat2.CoordinateSystem = EarthTOD;
Sat2.DisplayStateType = BrouwerMeanShort;
Sat2.BrouwerShortSMA  = 6938.137;
Sat2.BrouwerShortECC  = 0.0012;
Sat2.BrouwerShortINC  = 97.7876;
Sat2.BrouwerShortRAAN = 258.7256;
Sat2.BrouwerShortAOP  = 90;
Sat2.BrouwerShortMA   = 0;
Sat2.DryMass          = 395;
Sat2.Cd               = 2.2;
Sat2.Cr               = 1.3;
Sat2.DragArea         = 2.2;
Sat2.SRPArea          = 2.2;
Sat2.Tanks            = {Tank2};
Sat2.Thrusters        = {FeepT2, FeepNp2, FeepNm2};
Sat2.PowerSystem      = FeepPower;

%----------------------------------------
%---------- Hardware Components
%----------------------------------------

% Idealised constant power source, so that eclipses and sun angle never limit
% the FEEP thrust (the thrusters are modelled as ConstantThrustAndIsp).
Create NuclearPowerSystem FeepPower;
FeepPower.InitialMaxPower = 1;
FeepPower.AnnualDecayRate = 0;
FeepPower.Margin          = 0;
FeepPower.BusCoeff1       = 0.1;
FeepPower.BusCoeff2       = 0;
FeepPower.BusCoeff3       = 0;

Create ElectricTank Tank1;
Tank1.AllowNegativeFuelMass = false;
Tank1.FuelMass              = 5;

Create ElectricTank Tank2;
Tank2.AllowNegativeFuelMass = false;
Tank2.FuelMass              = 5;

% The out-of-plane thrusters fire along +/-Y, the default SecondDirection of GMAT
% hardware, which makes it print a harmless 'collinear' message at start-up; the
% SecondDirection is set to X to avoid that. It does not affect the thrust.
%
% Satellite 1: prograde tangential thruster and +N / -N out-of-plane thrusters.
% Thrust directions are fixed in the VNB frame (V = velocity, N = orbit normal).
% ConstantThrust is in Newton. It must match the ThrustN variable below.
Create ElectricThruster FeepT1;
FeepT1.CoordinateSystem   = Local;
FeepT1.Origin             = Earth;
FeepT1.Axes               = VNB;
FeepT1.ThrustDirection1   = 1;
FeepT1.ThrustDirection2   = 0;
FeepT1.ThrustDirection3   = 0;
FeepT1.DutyCycle          = 0;
FeepT1.DecrementMass      = true;
FeepT1.Tank               = {Tank1};
FeepT1.GravitationalAccel = 9.81;
FeepT1.ThrustModel        = ConstantThrustAndIsp;
FeepT1.MaximumUsablePower = 0.5;
FeepT1.MinimumUsablePower = 0.001;
FeepT1.ConstantThrust     = 0.004;
FeepT1.Isp                = 3000;

Create ElectricThruster FeepNp1;
FeepNp1.CoordinateSystem   = Local;
FeepNp1.Origin             = Earth;
FeepNp1.Axes               = VNB;
FeepNp1.ThrustDirection1   = 0;
FeepNp1.ThrustDirection2   = 1;
FeepNp1.ThrustDirection3   = 0;
FeepNp1.SecondDirectionX    = 1;
FeepNp1.SecondDirectionY    = 0;
FeepNp1.SecondDirectionZ    = 0;
FeepNp1.DutyCycle          = 0;
FeepNp1.DecrementMass      = true;
FeepNp1.Tank               = {Tank1};
FeepNp1.GravitationalAccel = 9.81;
FeepNp1.ThrustModel        = ConstantThrustAndIsp;
FeepNp1.MaximumUsablePower = 0.5;
FeepNp1.MinimumUsablePower = 0.001;
FeepNp1.ConstantThrust     = 0.004;
FeepNp1.Isp                = 3000;

Create ElectricThruster FeepNm1;
FeepNm1.CoordinateSystem   = Local;
FeepNm1.Origin             = Earth;
FeepNm1.Axes               = VNB;
FeepNm1.ThrustDirection1   = 0;
FeepNm1.ThrustDirection2   = -1;
FeepNm1.ThrustDirection3   = 0;
FeepNm1.SecondDirectionX    = 1;
FeepNm1.SecondDirectionY    = 0;
FeepNm1.SecondDirectionZ    = 0;
FeepNm1.DutyCycle          = 0;
FeepNm1.DecrementMass      = true;
FeepNm1.Tank               = {Tank1};
FeepNm1.GravitationalAccel = 9.81;
FeepNm1.ThrustModel        = ConstantThrustAndIsp;
FeepNm1.MaximumUsablePower = 0.5;
FeepNm1.MinimumUsablePower = 0.001;
FeepNm1.ConstantThrust     = 0.004;
FeepNm1.Isp                = 3000;

% Satellite 2: identical thruster set
Create ElectricThruster FeepT2;
FeepT2.CoordinateSystem   = Local;
FeepT2.Origin             = Earth;
FeepT2.Axes               = VNB;
FeepT2.ThrustDirection1   = 1;
FeepT2.ThrustDirection2   = 0;
FeepT2.ThrustDirection3   = 0;
FeepT2.DutyCycle          = 0;
FeepT2.DecrementMass      = true;
FeepT2.Tank               = {Tank2};
FeepT2.GravitationalAccel = 9.81;
FeepT2.ThrustModel        = ConstantThrustAndIsp;
FeepT2.MaximumUsablePower = 0.5;
FeepT2.MinimumUsablePower = 0.001;
FeepT2.ConstantThrust     = 0.004;
FeepT2.Isp                = 3000;

Create ElectricThruster FeepNp2;
FeepNp2.CoordinateSystem   = Local;
FeepNp2.Origin             = Earth;
FeepNp2.Axes               = VNB;
FeepNp2.ThrustDirection1   = 0;
FeepNp2.ThrustDirection2   = 1;
FeepNp2.ThrustDirection3   = 0;
FeepNp2.SecondDirectionX    = 1;
FeepNp2.SecondDirectionY    = 0;
FeepNp2.SecondDirectionZ    = 0;
FeepNp2.DutyCycle          = 0;
FeepNp2.DecrementMass      = true;
FeepNp2.Tank               = {Tank2};
FeepNp2.GravitationalAccel = 9.81;
FeepNp2.ThrustModel        = ConstantThrustAndIsp;
FeepNp2.MaximumUsablePower = 0.5;
FeepNp2.MinimumUsablePower = 0.001;
FeepNp2.ConstantThrust     = 0.004;
FeepNp2.Isp                = 3000;

Create ElectricThruster FeepNm2;
FeepNm2.CoordinateSystem   = Local;
FeepNm2.Origin             = Earth;
FeepNm2.Axes               = VNB;
FeepNm2.ThrustDirection1   = 0;
FeepNm2.ThrustDirection2   = -1;
FeepNm2.ThrustDirection3   = 0;
FeepNm2.SecondDirectionX    = 1;
FeepNm2.SecondDirectionY    = 0;
FeepNm2.SecondDirectionZ    = 0;
FeepNm2.DutyCycle          = 0;
FeepNm2.DecrementMass      = true;
FeepNm2.Tank               = {Tank2};
FeepNm2.GravitationalAccel = 9.81;
FeepNm2.ThrustModel        = ConstantThrustAndIsp;
FeepNm2.MaximumUsablePower = 0.5;
FeepNm2.MinimumUsablePower = 0.001;
FeepNm2.ConstantThrust     = 0.004;
FeepNm2.Isp                = 3000;

%----------------------------------------
%---------- Burns
%----------------------------------------

Create FiniteBurn Burn1;
Burn1.Thrusters = {FeepT1, FeepNp1, FeepNm1};

Create FiniteBurn Burn2;
Burn2.Thrusters = {FeepT2, FeepNp2, FeepNm2};

%----------------------------------------
%---------- ForceModels
%----------------------------------------

% 8x8 EGM96, Sun and Moon point masses, SRP, NRLMSISE-00 drag driven by the
% Schatten solar-cycle prediction (nominal cycle, nominal error model).
% Change SchattenErrorModel to 'PlusTwoSigma' / 'MinusTwoSigma' and SchattenTimingModel
% to 'EarlyCycle' / 'LateCycle' for high/low solar-activity scenarios.
Create ForceModel FormationFM;
FormationFM.CentralBody                      = Earth;
FormationFM.PrimaryBodies                    = {Earth};
FormationFM.PointMasses                      = {Sun, Luna};
FormationFM.SRP                              = On;
FormationFM.RelativisticCorrection           = Off;
FormationFM.ErrorControl                     = RSSStep;
FormationFM.GravityField.Earth.Degree        = 8;
FormationFM.GravityField.Earth.Order         = 8;
FormationFM.GravityField.Earth.PotentialFile = 'EGM96.cof';
FormationFM.GravityField.Earth.TideModel     = 'None';
FormationFM.SRP.Flux                         = 1367;
FormationFM.SRP.SRPModel                     = Spherical;
FormationFM.SRP.Nominal_Sun                  = 149597870.691;
FormationFM.Drag.AtmosphereModel             = NRLMSISE00;
FormationFM.Drag.HistoricWeatherSource       = 'ConstantFluxAndGeoMag';
FormationFM.Drag.PredictedWeatherSource      = 'SchattenFile';
FormationFM.Drag.SchattenFile                = 'SchattenPredict.txt';
FormationFM.Drag.SchattenErrorModel          = 'Nominal';
FormationFM.Drag.SchattenTimingModel         = 'NominalCycle';
FormationFM.Drag.F107                        = 150;
FormationFM.Drag.F107A                       = 150;
FormationFM.Drag.MagneticIndex               = 3;

%----------------------------------------
%---------- Propagators
%----------------------------------------

Create Propagator FormationProp;
FormationProp.FM                       = FormationFM;
FormationProp.Type                     = PrinceDormand78;
FormationProp.InitialStepSize          = 60;
FormationProp.Accuracy                 = 1e-10;
FormationProp.MinStep                  = 0.001;
FormationProp.MaxStep                  = 300;
FormationProp.MaxStepAttempts          = 50;
FormationProp.StopIfAccuracyIsViolated = true;

%----------------------------------------
%---------- Coordinate Systems
%----------------------------------------

% Earth true-of-date equator. The mean elements (inclination, RAAN) used for
% control are referred to it: relative to the J2000 equator the inclination
% oscillates by ~0.1 deg with the precession accumulated since 2000, which
% would be mistaken for a real drift.
Create CoordinateSystem EarthTOD;
EarthTOD.Origin = Earth;
EarthTOD.Axes   = TODEq;

% RTN frame centred on Sat1: X = radial, Y = along-track, Z = orbit normal.
% Sat2.Sat1RTN.Y is the along-track separation, Sat2.Sat1RTN.Z the normal one.
Create CoordinateSystem Sat1RTN;
Sat1RTN.Origin    = Sat1;
Sat1RTN.Axes      = ObjectReferenced;
Sat1RTN.XAxis     = R;
Sat1RTN.ZAxis     = N;
Sat1RTN.Primary   = Earth;
Sat1RTN.Secondary = Sat1;

%----------------------------------------
%---------- Variables
%----------------------------------------

% Design parameters
Create Variable ControlOn MissionDays MissionSecs MissionOrbits CycleOrbits CycleSecs;
Create Variable aRef eRef iRef aopRef raanRef;
Create Variable NAmp T0 TLow THigh TCenter VdT VtolT kappaT;
Create Variable ThrustN Isp0 g0;

% Controller tuning
Create Variable tauA tauI iDead iTol ffInit diBias eOmTol eOmRel iDead2 iAim aimSign startC diRem1 diRem2 absRem1 absRem2;

% Constants
Create Variable muE ReE J2E PiC;

% Initial geometry
Create Variable iRad sI cI dRaanRad dRaan du0;

% Time, cycle and orbit bookkeeping
Create Variable tNext tSim tDays nCyc nOrbCycle orbT orbDone orbNext finished iOrb iSeg;
Create Variable uTarget uNow1 uNow2 uErr uDotNom TnNom;

% Cycle measurements and commands (suffix 1 / 2 = satellite)
Create Variable aM1 aM2 iM1 iM2 raanM1 raanM2 eM1 eM2 aAvg1 aAvg2 iAvg1 iAvg2;
Create Variable sumA1 sumA2 sumI1 sumI2 aTmp iTmp;
Create Variable Trel Nrel Rrel Rng ANamp dRaanM dRaanDeg diM;
Create Variable diCmd iTgt2 eOm absEo nOmEv HoldSSO iDeadRel iAimRel;
Create Variable Tprev TdotM TdotDes dTe dANeed relMode doRel absTe CyclePrev dACmd aTgt1 aTgt2;
Create Variable nM1 nM2 uDot1 uDot2 uDotD1 uDotD2 sM1 sM2 s2M1 s2M2 vCirc1 vCirc2;
Create Variable mass1 mass2 fMax1 fMax2;
Create Variable delta1 delta2 absD1 absD2 ff1 ff2 fCmd1 fCmd2 dutyT1 dutyT2 Kp1 Kp2;
Create Variable diErr1 diErr2 absDi1 absDi2 camp1 camp2 sAsc1 sAsc2 dutyN1 dutyN2 diMax1 diMax2;
Create Variable aop1 aop2 ta1 ta2 uTmp1 uTmp2 cu1 cu2 s01 s02 tb1 tb2 segT sg;
Create Variable dvT1 dvN1 dvT2 dvN2 dvTot mProp1 mProp2 dvRkt1 dvRkt2 m01 m02;
Create Variable dutySumT1 dutySumT2 dutyMaxT1 dutyMaxT2 campCyc1 campCyc2;

% Compliance statistics
Create Variable TMin TMax ANMin ANMax RngMin dAMax1 dAMax2 nOutT nOutN nRel dEp absEp epMax;

%----------------------------------------
%---------- Subscribers
%----------------------------------------

Create ReportFile DailyReport;
DailyReport.Filename       = 'FormationSSO_FEEP_Daily.txt';
DailyReport.Precision      = 10;
DailyReport.WriteHeaders   = true;
DailyReport.LeftJustify    = On;
DailyReport.ZeroFill       = Off;
DailyReport.FixedWidth     = true;
DailyReport.ColumnWidth    = 20;
DailyReport.WriteReport    = true;

Create ReportFile SummaryReport;
SummaryReport.Filename     = 'FormationSSO_FEEP_Summary.txt';
SummaryReport.Precision    = 8;
SummaryReport.WriteHeaders = true;
SummaryReport.LeftJustify  = On;
SummaryReport.ZeroFill     = Off;
SummaryReport.FixedWidth   = true;
SummaryReport.ColumnWidth  = 20;
SummaryReport.WriteReport  = true;

%----------------------------------------
%---------- Mission Sequence
%----------------------------------------

BeginMissionSequence;

%---------------------------------------------------------------
%  Design parameters (edit here)
%---------------------------------------------------------------
ControlOn   = 1;         % 1 = controlled, 0 = free drift (no thrust at all)
HoldSSO     = 0;         % 1 = also hold the sun-synchronous inclination (and so the LTAN)
                         % 0 = no absolute inclination control: the orbit plane may
                         %     drift, only the formation geometry is kept
MissionDays = 1826;      % 5 years incl. one leap day (2028)
CycleOrbits = 15;        % control cycle = 15 nodal periods (~1.000 day)

% Reference mean orbit (Brouwer-Lyddane "short" mean elements, true-of-date)
aRef    = 6938.137;      % km, 560 km altitude
eRef    = 0.0012;        % frozen-orbit eccentricity
aopRef  = 90;            % deg, frozen-orbit argument of perigee
iRef    = 97.653;        % deg, tuned for exactly sun-synchronous nodal rate
raanRef = 258.7256;      % deg, LTAN 10:30 at 01 Jan 2027 (centre of the pair)

% Formation requirement (Sat2 relative to Sat1, RTN)
NAmp    = 200;           % km, normal separation amplitude
T0      = 525;           % km, initial along-track separation (mid corridor)
TLow    = 100;           % km, reverse drift below this (requirement: 50)
THigh   = 950;           % km, reverse drift above this (requirement: 1000)
TCenter = 525;           % km, stop the reversal drift when back at this value
VdT     = 1.5;           % km/day, drift rate used to come back from a limit
VtolT   = 0.4;           % km/day, tolerance on the commanded drift rate
kappaT  = 0.3;           % fraction of the needed SMA change commanded per cycle

% FEEP assumptions (ThrustN must equal ConstantThrust above, Isp0 the Isp)
ThrustN = 0.004;         % N per thruster (a cluster of four 1 mN FEEP heads)
Isp0    = 3000;          % s
g0      = 9.81;          % m/s^2, same value as the thrusters' GravitationalAccel

% Controller tuning
tauA    = 129600;        % s, altitude loop time constant (1.5 day)
tauI    = 1296000;       % s, altitude loop integral time (15 day, overdamped)
ffInit  = 1.0e-7;        % m/s^2, first guess of the drag make-up acceleration
iDead   = 0.01;          % deg, start an inclination campaign above this error
iTol    = 0.0005;        % deg, a campaign ends when the commanded change left is below this
iAim    = 0.005;         % deg, a campaign aims this far past the reference (against the drift)
iDeadRel = 0.001;        % deg, HoldSSO = 0: Sat2 corrects when its inclination differs
                         %      from Sat1's by more than this
iAimRel = 0.0005;        % deg, ... and aims this far past Sat1's inclination
eOmTol  = 0.04;          % deg, tolerated drift of the RAAN offset (about 5 km of N amplitude)
diBias  = 0.004;         % deg, differential inclination used to steer the RAAN offset back

% Constants (EGM96)
muE = 398600.4415;
ReE = 6378.1363;
J2E = 1.08262668e-3;
PiC = 3.14159265358979;

%---------------------------------------------------------------
%  Initial formation geometry
%---------------------------------------------------------------
MissionSecs = MissionDays * 86400;
iRad     = degToRad(iRef);
sI       = sin(iRad);
cI       = cos(iRad);
dRaanRad = NAmp / (aRef * sI);
dRaan    = radToDeg(dRaanRad);
du0      = radToDeg(T0 / aRef) - dRaan * cI;

Sat1.BrouwerShortSMA  = aRef;
Sat1.BrouwerShortECC  = eRef;
Sat1.BrouwerShortINC  = iRef;
Sat1.BrouwerShortRAAN = raanRef - 0.5 * dRaan;
Sat1.BrouwerShortAOP  = aopRef;
Sat1.BrouwerShortMA   = 0;

Sat2.BrouwerShortSMA  = aRef;
Sat2.BrouwerShortECC  = eRef;
Sat2.BrouwerShortINC  = iRef;
Sat2.BrouwerShortRAAN = raanRef + 0.5 * dRaan;
Sat2.BrouwerShortAOP  = aopRef;
Sat2.BrouwerShortMA   = du0;

%---------------------------------------------------------------
%  Initialise controller state and statistics
%---------------------------------------------------------------
tSim = 0;
nCyc = 0;
orbDone = 0;
finished = 0;
dACmd = 0;
diCmd = 0;
nOmEv = 0;
relMode = 0;
Tprev = T0;
CyclePrev = 86400;
ff1 = ffInit;
ff2 = ffInit;
camp1 = 0;
camp2 = 0;
diRem1 = 0;
diRem2 = 0;
dvT1 = 0;
dvN1 = 0;
dvT2 = 0;
dvN2 = 0;
dutySumT1 = 0;
dutySumT2 = 0;
dutyMaxT1 = 0;
dutyMaxT2 = 0;
campCyc1 = 0;
campCyc2 = 0;
TMin = 1e9;
TMax = -1e9;
ANMin = 1e9;
ANMax = -1e9;
RngMin = 1e9;
dAMax1 = 0;
dAMax2 = 0;
nOutT = 0;
nOutN = 0;
nRel = 0;
epMax = 0;
m01 = Sat1.TotalMass;
m02 = Sat2.TotalMass;

% Mean elements fed to the controller are averaged over the 15 orbits of the
% previous cycle (sampled once per orbit at the same argument of latitude).
% This removes the tesseral-harmonic short-period terms (tens of metres in SMA),
% which would otherwise look like noise to the controller.
aAvg1 = Sat1.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortSMA;
aAvg2 = Sat2.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortSMA;
iAvg1 = Sat1.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortINC;
iAvg2 = Sat2.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortINC;

% Argument of latitude at which the cycle starts, kept constant by adjusting
% the length of each cycle. Mission length in orbits from the nominal period.
aop1 = Sat1.EarthTOD.AOP;
ta1  = Sat1.Earth.TA;
uTmp1 = aop1 + ta1;
uTarget = mod(uTmp1, 360);
nM1     = sqrt(muE / (aRef*aRef*aRef));
s2M1    = sI * sI;
uDotNom = nM1 * (1 + J2E * (ReE/aRef) * (ReE/aRef) * (4.5 - 6 * s2M1));
TnNom   = 2 * PiC / uDotNom;
MissionOrbits = fix(MissionSecs / TnNom);

While finished == 0

   %------------------------------------------------------------
   %  1. Measurements: relative RTN state, mean elements for the log
   %------------------------------------------------------------
   tDays  = tSim / 86400;
   aM1    = Sat1.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortSMA;
   aM2    = Sat2.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortSMA;
   iM1    = Sat1.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortINC;
   iM2    = Sat2.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortINC;
   raanM1 = Sat1.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortRAAN;
   raanM2 = Sat2.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortRAAN;
   eM1    = Sat1.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortECC;
   eM2    = Sat2.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortECC;
   % The satellites are propagated one after the other for the same time, so
   % they are at the same epoch whenever the RTN state is read; epMax checks it.
   dEp    = (Sat2.A1ModJulian - Sat1.A1ModJulian) * 86400;
   absEp  = abs(dEp);
   If absEp > epMax
      epMax = absEp;
   EndIf;
   Rrel   = Sat2.Sat1RTN.X;
   Trel   = Sat2.Sat1RTN.Y;
   Nrel   = Sat2.Sat1RTN.Z;
   Rng    = sqrt(Rrel*Rrel + Trel*Trel + Nrel*Nrel);
   mass1  = Sat1.TotalMass;
   mass2  = Sat2.TotalMass;

   % Normal-separation amplitude from the mean-element differences
   dRaanM = raanM2 - raanM1;
   If dRaanM > 180
      dRaanM = dRaanM - 360;
   EndIf;
   If dRaanM < -180
      dRaanM = dRaanM + 360;
   EndIf;
   dRaanDeg = dRaanM;
   diM    = degToRad(iAvg2 - iAvg1);
   dRaanM = degToRad(dRaanM);
   sM1    = sin(degToRad(iAvg1));
   ANamp  = aAvg1 * sqrt(diM*diM + sM1*sM1*dRaanM*dRaanM);

   % Statistics
   If Trel < TMin
      TMin = Trel;
   EndIf;
   If Trel > TMax
      TMax = Trel;
   EndIf;
   If ANamp < ANMin
      ANMin = ANamp;
   EndIf;
   If ANamp > ANMax
      ANMax = ANamp;
   EndIf;
   If Rng < RngMin
      RngMin = Rng;
   EndIf;
   If Trel < 50
      nOutT = nOutT + 1;
   EndIf;
   If Trel > 1000
      nOutT = nOutT + 1;
   EndIf;
   If ANamp < 180
      nOutN = nOutN + 1;
   EndIf;
   If ANamp > 220
      nOutN = nOutN + 1;
   EndIf;

   %------------------------------------------------------------
   %  2. Cycle length: 15 nodal periods, phase locked to Sat1
   %------------------------------------------------------------
   orbNext = orbDone + CycleOrbits;
   nOrbCycle = CycleOrbits;
   If orbNext > MissionOrbits
      nOrbCycle = MissionOrbits - orbDone;
   EndIf;
   If nOrbCycle < 1
      nOrbCycle = 1;
   EndIf;
   nM1     = sqrt(muE / (aAvg1*aAvg1*aAvg1));
   nM2     = sqrt(muE / (aAvg2*aAvg2*aAvg2));
   sM1     = sin(degToRad(iAvg1));
   sM2     = sin(degToRad(iAvg2));
   s2M1    = sM1 * sM1;
   s2M2    = sM2 * sM2;
   uDot1   = nM1 * (1 + J2E * (ReE/aAvg1) * (ReE/aAvg1) * (4.5 - 6 * s2M1));
   uDot2   = nM2 * (1 + J2E * (ReE/aAvg2) * (ReE/aAvg2) * (4.5 - 6 * s2M2));
   uDotD1  = radToDeg(uDot1);
   uDotD2  = radToDeg(uDot2);
   aop1    = Sat1.EarthTOD.AOP;
   ta1     = Sat1.Earth.TA;
   uTmp1   = aop1 + ta1;
   uNow1   = mod(uTmp1, 360);
   aop2    = Sat2.EarthTOD.AOP;
   ta2     = Sat2.Earth.TA;
   uTmp2   = aop2 + ta2;
   uNow2   = mod(uTmp2, 360);
   uErr    = uTarget - uNow1;
   If uErr > 180
      uErr = uErr - 360;
   EndIf;
   If uErr < -180
      uErr = uErr + 360;
   EndIf;
   CycleSecs = (360 * nOrbCycle + uErr) / uDotD1;
   orbT      = CycleSecs / nOrbCycle;

   %------------------------------------------------------------
   %  3. Relative along-track logic (drift reversal with hysteresis)
   %     Uses the measured drift rate, not absolute SMA differences.
   %------------------------------------------------------------
   TdotM = 0;
   If nCyc > 0
      TdotM = (Trel - Tprev) / (CyclePrev / 86400);
   EndIf;
   TdotDes = 0;
   doRel = 0;
   If relMode == 0
      If Trel > THigh
         relMode = -1;
         doRel = 1;
      EndIf;
      If Trel < TLow
         relMode = 1;
         doRel = 1;
      EndIf;
   Else
      If relMode < 0
         If Trel < TCenter
            relMode = 0;
            doRel = 1;
         EndIf;
      Else
         If Trel > TCenter
            relMode = 0;
            doRel = 1;
         EndIf;
      EndIf;
   EndIf;
   If relMode < 0
      TdotDes = -VdT;
   EndIf;
   If relMode > 0
      TdotDes = VdT;
   EndIf;
   dTe = TdotDes - TdotM;
   absTe = abs(dTe);
   If relMode ~= 0
      If absTe > VtolT
         doRel = 1;
      EndIf;
   EndIf;
   If doRel == 1
      % T-dot = -1.5 n da  ->  SMA change needed for the commanded drift rate
      dANeed = -dTe / (86400 * 1.5 * nM1);
      dACmd  = dACmd + kappaT * dANeed;
      nRel   = nRel + 1;
      If dACmd > 0.2
         dACmd = 0.2;
      EndIf;
      If dACmd < -0.2
         dACmd = -0.2;
      EndIf;
   EndIf;
   Tprev     = Trel;
   CyclePrev = CycleSecs;
   % The thrusters are prograde only, so a relative SMA offset is made by
   % raising whichever satellite has to be higher.
   aTgt1 = aRef;
   aTgt2 = aRef;
   If dACmd > 0
      aTgt2 = aRef + dACmd;
   EndIf;
   If dACmd < 0
      aTgt1 = aRef - dACmd;
   EndIf;

   %------------------------------------------------------------
   %  4. Tangential thrust command (PI on mean SMA, prograde only)
   %------------------------------------------------------------
   Kp1    = nM1 / (2 * tauA);
   Kp2    = nM2 / (2 * tauA);
   fMax1  = ThrustN / mass1;
   fMax2  = ThrustN / mass2;

   delta1 = (aAvg1 - aTgt1) * 1000;
   delta2 = (aAvg2 - aTgt2) * 1000;
   absD1  = abs(delta1);
   absD2  = abs(delta2);
   If absD1 > dAMax1
      dAMax1 = absD1;
   EndIf;
   If absD2 > dAMax2
      dAMax2 = absD2;
   EndIf;

   ff1 = ff1 - (Kp1 / tauI) * delta1 * CycleSecs;
   ff2 = ff2 - (Kp2 / tauI) * delta2 * CycleSecs;
   If ff1 < 0
      ff1 = 0;
   EndIf;
   If ff1 > fMax1
      ff1 = fMax1;
   EndIf;
   If ff2 < 0
      ff2 = 0;
   EndIf;
   If ff2 > fMax2
      ff2 = fMax2;
   EndIf;
   fCmd1 = ff1 - Kp1 * delta1;
   fCmd2 = ff2 - Kp2 * delta2;
   If fCmd1 < 0
      fCmd1 = 0;
   EndIf;
   If fCmd1 > fMax1
      fCmd1 = fMax1;
   EndIf;
   If fCmd2 < 0
      fCmd2 = 0;
   EndIf;
   If fCmd2 > fMax2
      fCmd2 = fMax2;
   EndIf;
   dutyT1 = fCmd1 / fMax1;
   dutyT2 = fCmd2 / fMax2;

   %------------------------------------------------------------
   %  5. Inclination (out-of-plane) command with hysteresis
   %------------------------------------------------------------
   % Relative node control. The inclination campaigns of the two satellites are
   % coordinated (both run when Sat1 reaches its limit, or when Sat2 reaches
   % twice the limit), so the two planes keep precessing together. A small differential inclination is applied only
   % if the RAAN offset, hence the N amplitude, has drifted anyway.
   % d(RAAN rate)/d(inc) is positive, so a lower inc of Sat2 shrinks the offset.
   eOm   = dRaanDeg - dRaan;
   eOmRel = 0.25 * eOmTol;
   absEo = abs(eOm);
   If diCmd == 0
      If absEo > eOmTol
         nOmEv = nOmEv + 1;
         diCmd = diBias;
         If eOm > 0
            diCmd = -diBias;
         EndIf;
      EndIf;
   Else
      If absEo < eOmRel
         diCmd = 0;
      EndIf;
   EndIf;
   iTgt2  = iRef + diCmd;
   If HoldSSO == 0
      iTgt2 = iAvg1 + diCmd;
   EndIf;
   diErr1 = iAvg1 - iRef;
   diErr2 = iAvg2 - iTgt2;
   absDi1 = abs(diErr1);
   absDi2 = abs(diErr2);

   % With HoldSSO = 0 the satellites follow Sat1's inclination: only Sat2 runs
   % campaigns, relative to Sat1, and Sat1 never does.
   % A campaign is planned open loop: when a limit is reached, the change needed
   % to get to the aim point is commanded over as many cycles as it takes, and
   % the commanded change (not the lagging measurement) is counted down.
   % Both satellites run it together, started by Sat1 reaching iDead, or by
   % Sat2 reaching twice that. The aim point is iAim beyond the reference, on
   % the side opposite to the drift, which halves the number of campaigns.
   iDead2 = 2 * iDead;
   startC = 0;
   aimSign = 0;
   If camp1 == 0
      If camp2 == 0
         If HoldSSO == 1
            If absDi1 > iDead
               startC = 1;
               aimSign = 1;
               If diErr1 > 0
                  aimSign = -1;
               EndIf;
            EndIf;
            If absDi2 > iDead2
               startC = 1;
               aimSign = 1;
               If diErr2 > 0
                  aimSign = -1;
               EndIf;
            EndIf;
         Else
            % Only the inclination of Sat2 relative to Sat1 is controlled.
            If absDi2 > iDeadRel
               startC = 1;
               aimSign = 1;
               If diErr2 > 0
                  aimSign = -1;
               EndIf;
            EndIf;
         EndIf;
      EndIf;
   EndIf;
   If startC == 1
      If HoldSSO == 1
         camp1  = 1;
         camp2  = 1;
         diRem1 = -diErr1 + aimSign * iAim;
         diRem2 = -diErr2 + aimSign * iAim;
      Else
         camp2  = 1;
         diRem2 = -diErr2 + aimSign * iAimRel;
      EndIf;
   EndIf;

   % Orbit-averaged di/dt of a sign(cos u) out-of-plane thrust: (2/pi) fN / v
   vCirc1 = sqrt(muE / aAvg1) * 1000;
   vCirc2 = sqrt(muE / aAvg2) * 1000;
   diMax1 = radToDeg((2 / PiC) * (fMax1 / vCirc1) * CycleSecs);
   diMax2 = radToDeg((2 / PiC) * (fMax2 / vCirc2) * CycleSecs);
   dutyN1 = 0;
   dutyN2 = 0;
   sAsc1  = 1;
   sAsc2  = 1;
   absRem1 = abs(diRem1);
   absRem2 = abs(diRem2);
   If absRem1 < iTol
      camp1 = 0;
   EndIf;
   If absRem2 < iTol
      camp2 = 0;
   EndIf;
   If camp1 == 1
      dutyN1 = absRem1 / diMax1;
      If dutyN1 > 1
         dutyN1 = 1;
      EndIf;
      If diRem1 < 0
         sAsc1 = -1;
         diRem1 = diRem1 + dutyN1 * diMax1;
      Else
         diRem1 = diRem1 - dutyN1 * diMax1;
      EndIf;
   EndIf;
   If camp2 == 1
      dutyN2 = absRem2 / diMax2;
      If dutyN2 > 1
         dutyN2 = 1;
      EndIf;
      If diRem2 < 0
         sAsc2 = -1;
         diRem2 = diRem2 + dutyN2 * diMax2;
      Else
         diRem2 = diRem2 - dutyN2 * diMax2;
      EndIf;
   EndIf;

   If ControlOn == 0
      dutyT1 = 0;
      dutyT2 = 0;
      dutyN1 = 0;
      dutyN2 = 0;
      camp1  = 0;
      camp2  = 0;
   EndIf;

   %------------------------------------------------------------
   %  6. Log
   %------------------------------------------------------------
   Report DailyReport tDays uNow1 aAvg1 aAvg2 iAvg1 iAvg2 raanM1 raanM2 eM1 eM2 Rrel Trel Nrel Rng ANamp dACmd TdotM diCmd dutyT1 dutyT2 dutyN1 dutyN2 dvT1 dvN1 dvT2 dvN2 mass1 mass2 CycleSecs;

   % The last pass (all orbits done) only measures and logs.
   If orbDone >= MissionOrbits
      finished = 1;
   EndIf;

   If finished == 0

      dutySumT1 = dutySumT1 + dutyT1;
      dutySumT2 = dutySumT2 + dutyT2;
      If dutyT1 > dutyMaxT1
         dutyMaxT1 = dutyT1;
      EndIf;
      If dutyT2 > dutyMaxT2
         dutyMaxT2 = dutyT2;
      EndIf;

      %---------------------------------------------------------
      %  7. Propagate Sat1 one cycle (continuous finite burns)
      %---------------------------------------------------------
      sumA1 = 0;
      sumI1 = 0;
      iOrb  = 1;
      Sat1.FeepT1.DutyCycle  = dutyT1;
      Sat1.FeepNp1.DutyCycle = 0;
      Sat1.FeepNm1.DutyCycle = 0;
      If camp1 == 0
         BeginFiniteBurn Burn1(Sat1);
         While iOrb <= nOrbCycle
            Propagate FormationProp(Sat1) {Sat1.ElapsedSecs = orbT};
            aTmp  = Sat1.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortSMA;
            iTmp  = Sat1.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortINC;
            sumA1 = sumA1 + aTmp;
            sumI1 = sumI1 + iTmp;
            iOrb  = iOrb + 1;
         EndWhile;
         EndFiniteBurn Burn1(Sat1);
      Else
         % Inclination campaign. The out-of-plane thrust follows sign(cos u): it
         % is flipped at the polar points (u = 90 and 270 deg). Each orbit is
         % split into three segments between those switching points.
         campCyc1 = campCyc1 + 1;
         cu1  = cos(degToRad(uNow1));
         s01  = sAsc1;
         If cu1 < 0
            s01 = -sAsc1;
         EndIf;
         tb1  = 450 - uNow1;
         tb1  = mod(tb1, 180);
         tb1  = tb1 / uDotD1;
         While iOrb <= nOrbCycle
            iSeg = 1;
            While iSeg <= 3
               segT = 0.5 * orbT;
               sg   = -s01;
               If iSeg == 1
                  segT = tb1;
                  sg   = s01;
               EndIf;
               If iSeg == 3
                  segT = 0.5 * orbT - tb1;
                  sg   = s01;
               EndIf;
               If segT > 0.5
                  If sg > 0
                     Sat1.FeepNp1.DutyCycle = dutyN1;
                     Sat1.FeepNm1.DutyCycle = 0;
                  Else
                     Sat1.FeepNp1.DutyCycle = 0;
                     Sat1.FeepNm1.DutyCycle = dutyN1;
                  EndIf;
                  BeginFiniteBurn Burn1(Sat1);
                  Propagate FormationProp(Sat1) {Sat1.ElapsedSecs = segT};
                  EndFiniteBurn Burn1(Sat1);
                  dvN1 = dvN1 + dutyN1 * fMax1 * segT;
               EndIf;
               iSeg = iSeg + 1;
            EndWhile;
            aTmp  = Sat1.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortSMA;
            iTmp  = Sat1.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortINC;
            sumA1 = sumA1 + aTmp;
            sumI1 = sumI1 + iTmp;
            iOrb  = iOrb + 1;
         EndWhile;
         Sat1.FeepNp1.DutyCycle = 0;
         Sat1.FeepNm1.DutyCycle = 0;
      EndIf;
      dvT1  = dvT1 + dutyT1 * fMax1 * CycleSecs;
      aAvg1 = sumA1 / nOrbCycle;
      iAvg1 = sumI1 / nOrbCycle;

      %---------------------------------------------------------
      %  8. Propagate Sat2 one cycle
      %---------------------------------------------------------
      sumA2 = 0;
      sumI2 = 0;
      iOrb  = 1;
      Sat2.FeepT2.DutyCycle  = dutyT2;
      Sat2.FeepNp2.DutyCycle = 0;
      Sat2.FeepNm2.DutyCycle = 0;
      If camp2 == 0
         BeginFiniteBurn Burn2(Sat2);
         While iOrb <= nOrbCycle
            Propagate FormationProp(Sat2) {Sat2.ElapsedSecs = orbT};
            aTmp  = Sat2.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortSMA;
            iTmp  = Sat2.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortINC;
            sumA2 = sumA2 + aTmp;
            sumI2 = sumI2 + iTmp;
            iOrb  = iOrb + 1;
         EndWhile;
         EndFiniteBurn Burn2(Sat2);
      Else
         campCyc2 = campCyc2 + 1;
         cu2  = cos(degToRad(uNow2));
         s02  = sAsc2;
         If cu2 < 0
            s02 = -sAsc2;
         EndIf;
         tb2  = 450 - uNow2;
         tb2  = mod(tb2, 180);
         tb2  = tb2 / uDotD2;
         While iOrb <= nOrbCycle
            iSeg = 1;
            While iSeg <= 3
               segT = 0.5 * orbT;
               sg   = -s02;
               If iSeg == 1
                  segT = tb2;
                  sg   = s02;
               EndIf;
               If iSeg == 3
                  segT = 0.5 * orbT - tb2;
                  sg   = s02;
               EndIf;
               If segT > 0.5
                  If sg > 0
                     Sat2.FeepNp2.DutyCycle = dutyN2;
                     Sat2.FeepNm2.DutyCycle = 0;
                  Else
                     Sat2.FeepNp2.DutyCycle = 0;
                     Sat2.FeepNm2.DutyCycle = dutyN2;
                  EndIf;
                  BeginFiniteBurn Burn2(Sat2);
                  Propagate FormationProp(Sat2) {Sat2.ElapsedSecs = segT};
                  EndFiniteBurn Burn2(Sat2);
                  dvN2 = dvN2 + dutyN2 * fMax2 * segT;
               EndIf;
               iSeg = iSeg + 1;
            EndWhile;
            aTmp  = Sat2.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortSMA;
            iTmp  = Sat2.EarthTOD.BrouwerShortINC;
            sumA2 = sumA2 + aTmp;
            sumI2 = sumI2 + iTmp;
            iOrb  = iOrb + 1;
         EndWhile;
         Sat2.FeepNp2.DutyCycle = 0;
         Sat2.FeepNm2.DutyCycle = 0;
      EndIf;
      dvT2  = dvT2 + dutyT2 * fMax2 * CycleSecs;
      aAvg2 = sumA2 / nOrbCycle;
      iAvg2 = sumI2 / nOrbCycle;

      tSim    = tSim + CycleSecs;
      orbDone = orbDone + nOrbCycle;
      nCyc    = nCyc + 1;
   EndIf;
EndWhile;

%---------------------------------------------------------------
%  Summary
%---------------------------------------------------------------
mProp1    = m01 - Sat1.TotalMass;
mProp2    = m02 - Sat2.TotalMass;
dvRkt1    = Isp0 * g0 * log(m01 / Sat1.TotalMass);
dvRkt2    = Isp0 * g0 * log(m02 / Sat2.TotalMass);
dvTot     = dvT1 + dvN1 + dvT2 + dvN2;
dutySumT1 = dutySumT1 / nCyc;
dutySumT2 = dutySumT2 / nCyc;

Report SummaryReport MissionDays tDays nCyc dvT1 dvN1 dvT2 dvN2 dvTot dvRkt1 dvRkt2 mProp1 mProp2;
Report SummaryReport dutySumT1 dutyMaxT1 dutySumT2 dutyMaxT2 campCyc1 campCyc2 dAMax1 dAMax2 nRel nOmEv;
Report SummaryReport TMin TMax ANMin ANMax RngMin nOutT nOutN epMax;
